@dialogue 1
@text rich
@document harbor.showcase
@characters Cast "characters"
@context "story"
@actions "actions"
@events "events"
@bind name context.name
@entry quick
[start]
// @id crossing.open
Cast.Guide: You came back, %{name}. I left the lamp burning. [pause=0.35]I wasn't certain you would.
@expression worried
@speech character
@emit shown 0 signal [id:crossing.open.shown] {"phase":"shown"}
@emit revealed 0.1 signal [id:crossing.open.revealed] {"phase":"revealed"}
// @id crossing.weather
Cast.Guide: There is a boat beyond the breakwater. No running lights. Every few minutes, someone rings a bell.
@speech character
// @id crossing.arrival
Cast.Courier: Three rings. Then two. The same as the old ferry. I know because I used to count them from my window.
@speech character
// @id crossing.question
Cast.Guide: Before we do anything foolish, tell me what you need to know.
@speech character
// @id crossing.start.choice.1
-> Who is on the boat? [target:passengers]
// @id crossing.start.choice.2
-> Why is the lighthouse dark? [target:lamp]
// @id crossing.start.choice.3
-> Show me the channel chart. [target:chart]
// @id crossing.start.choice.4
-> We should decide what to do. [target:decision]
[hub]
// @id crossing.hub
Cast.Guide: Ask. We still have a little time.
@speech character
// @id crossing.hub.choice.1
-> Who is on the boat? [target:passengers]
// @id crossing.hub.choice.2
-> Why is the lighthouse dark? [target:lamp]
// @id crossing.hub.choice.3
-> Show me the channel chart. [target:chart]
// @id crossing.hub.choice.4
-> We should decide what to do. [target:decision]
// @id crossing.hub.choice.5
-> Repeat the safe route. [target:chart_reply]
@visible locals.charted
@fallback decision
[passengers]
// @id crossing.passengers.1
Cast.Courier: My sister took that ferry six years ago. So did half the people whose names are on the wall.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.passengers.2
Cast.Guide: We never found the hull. That is not the same as saying the passengers survived.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.passengers.3
Cast.Courier: I know the difference between hope and evidence. I just don't like it very much.
@speech character
// @id crossing.passengers.choice.1
-> Ask another question. [target:hub]
// @id crossing.passengers.choice.2
-> Tell Ivo you believe him. [target:trust]
[trust]
@action remember [id:crossing.trust.action] [success:trust_reply] [failure:hub] {"topic":"trust"}
[trust_reply]
// @id crossing.trust.reply
Cast.Courier: Thank you. You don't have to believe every word. Just don't make me listen to that bell alone.
@expression happy
@speech character
// @id crossing.trust_reply.choice.1
-> Return to Mara. [target:hub]
[lamp]
// @id crossing.lamp.1
Cast.Guide: The lens is intact. The keeper isn't. My hands shake when I climb the last flight of stairs.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.lamp.2
Cast.Guide: People think a lighthouse is a promise that the sea is safe. It isn't. It's a promise that somebody is watching.
@speech character
// @id crossing.lamp.3
Cast.Courier: Then let somebody else watch tonight.
@speech character
// @id crossing.lamp.choice.1
-> Ask another question. [target:hub]
// @id crossing.lamp.choice.2
-> We can light it together. [target:decision]
[chart]
// @id crossing.chart.1
Cast.Guide: Here. The wide channel is silted up. The narrow one follows a seam of pale stone under the water.
@speech character
// @id crossing.chart.2
Cast.Guide: Look for [em]three white markers[/em]. Keep the last one on your left. Everything else on this chart is a warning.
@speech character
// @id crossing.chart.choice.1
-> Memorize the safe passage. [target:remember_chart]
// @id crossing.chart.choice.2
-> Put the chart away. [target:hub]
[remember_chart]
@action remember [id:crossing.chart.action] [success:chart_reply] [failure:hub] {"topic":"chart"}
[chart_reply]
// @id crossing.chart.reply
Cast.Courier: Three white markers. Last one on the left. I'll say it until one of us stops being afraid.
@expression happy
@speech character
// @id crossing.chart_reply.choice.1
-> Return to the question at hand. [target:hub]
[decision]
// @id crossing.decision
Cast.Guide: Once we turn the light toward them, there is no calling it back. Are we guiding them in, going out, or leaving the sea to keep its secrets?
@expression resolved
@speech character
// @id crossing.decision.choice.1
-> Light the beacon. Guide them home. [target:beacon_route]
// @id crossing.decision.choice.2
-> Take the skiff through the narrow channel. [target:skiff_route]
@enabled locals.charted and context.permit
// @id crossing.skiff.reason
@reason Study the chart and obtain a harbor permit. G toggles the permit for this demo.
// @id crossing.decision.choice.3
-> Leave the light dark tonight. [target:dark_route]
// @id crossing.decision.choice.4
-> I still have questions. [target:hub]
@fallback hub
[beacon_route]
// @id crossing.beacon.1
Cast.Guide: Take the lower handle. Slowly. The mechanism is older than either of us, and much less forgiving.
@speech character
// @id crossing.beacon.2
: Together, you turn the wheel. A thin bar of light crosses the room. Then the glass. Then the sea.
@speech off
// @id crossing.beacon.3
Cast.Robot: [style=radio]Channel open.[/style] Incoming vessel, identify yourself.
@speech character
@emit shown 0.2 signal [id:crossing.radio.shown] {"phase":"shown"}
// @id crossing.beacon_route.choice.1
-> Listen. [target:signal_wait]
[signal_wait]
@wait 0.8 [target:signal_reply]
[signal_reply]
// @id crossing.signal.reply
Cast.Robot: Passenger ferry, last transmission. Engine failure. We are leaving the ship. If this reaches the harbor... tell them we tried.
@voice {"cue":"greeting","sourceLocale":"en","fallback":"source"}
// @id crossing.signal.after
Cast.Courier: Not a voice. A recording. It has been calling for someone all this time.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.signal_reply.choice.1
-> Stay beside Ivo. [target:trust_variant]
[trust_variant]
@branch locals.trusted [target:trusted_end] [else:reserved_end]
[trusted_end]
// @id crossing.trusted.1
Cast.Courier: You said you believed me. I think I needed that more than I needed to be right.
@expression happy
@speech character
// @id crossing.trusted.2
Cast.Guide: The boat reaches the harbor at dawn. Empty, but not lost. We can finally put a date beneath those names. (end)
@expression happy
@speech character
[reserved_end]
// @id crossing.reserved.1
Cast.Courier: I should go and tell the others. They'll want to see it before the morning crowd arrives.
@speech character
// @id crossing.reserved.2
Cast.Guide: At dawn the empty ferry comes home. Some answers are smaller than the questions that bring us to them. (end)
@speech character
[skiff_route]
// @id crossing.skiff.1
Cast.Courier: Three white markers. Last one on the left. See? I was listening.
@expression happy
@speech character
// @id crossing.skiff.2
Cast.Guide: Take my coat. It has brought back everyone who borrowed it. That is not a guarantee, but it is a very good coat.
@expression happy
@speech character
// @id crossing.skiff.3
: The harbor falls quiet behind you. [style=wave]One white marker. Two. Three.[/style] On the ferry's deck, a bell moves in the wind.
@speech off
// @id crossing.skiff.4
Cast.Courier: Her scarf. Still tied to the rail. She said she would leave it there so I could find her boat.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.skiff.5
: You bring the scarf home. By morning, the harbor has stopped waiting for a miracle and started remembering a person. (end)
@speech off
[dark_route]
// @id crossing.dark.1
Cast.Courier: I won't pretend I understand. But I won't take the skiff without you, either.
@expression worried
@speech character
// @id crossing.dark.2
Cast.Guide: Staying is a decision too. We will keep watch until morning. Both of us.
@speech character
// @id crossing.dark.3
: At sunrise, there is no boat. Only the faint impression of a bell, and three people who heard it together. (end)
@speech off
[quick]
// @id harbor.welcome
Cast.Guide: Welcome to [em]Beacon Harbor[/em], %{name}. [style=wave]The tide is turning.[/style]
@speech character
@expression happy
@emit shown 0 signal [id:harbor.shown] {"phase":"shown"}
@emit revealed 0.1 signal [id:harbor.revealed] {"phase":"revealed"}
// @id harbor.recording
Cast.Robot: Radio check. This synthetic recording stands in for a full voice line.
@voice {"cue":"greeting","sourceLocale":"en","fallback":"source"}
// @id harbor.collect
-> Collect the harbor token [target:collect]
@enabled context.permit
// @id harbor.reason
@reason A harbor permit is required.
// @id harbor.leave
-> Watch the tide instead [target:wait]
@fallback failed
[collect]
@action collect [id:harbor.collect.action] [success:wait] [failure:failed] {"amount":1}
[wait]
@wait 0.5 [target:done]
[done]
// @id harbor.done
Cast.Guide: [style=warning]Stay curious.[/style] Your next crossing is waiting. (end)
@speech character
[failed]
// @id harbor.failed
Cast.Guide: The token could not be collected. (end)
